    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// An analyst may approve, correct, reject or defer, and the answer is read from the API —\n// `Verify Resolution` — not from the resume webhook's body. Until v1.1.0 this node read\n// `resolution` off the Wait node's output, which is the whole webhook request\n// ({ headers, body, ... }); the field was never at the top level, so every resumed run\n// took the halt branch. And a body is whatever whoever reached the webhook sent.\n//\n// Three outcomes, not two. `deferred` used to join `rejected` on the halt branch and move\n// the claim to `rejected` — a terminal state — for a decision that means \"look again\n// later\". A deferral now ends the run and leaves the claim where it is.\nconst v = $input.first().json;\nlet decision = 'defer';\nif (v.may_continue === true) decision = 'continue';\nelse if (v.resolution === 'rejected') decision = 'reject';\nreturn [{ json: Object.assign({}, v, { decision: decision }) }];"
      },
      "id": "apply-resolution",
      "name": "Apply Resolution",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1420,
        140
      ]
    },
